WEBVTT

00:24.791 --> 00:26.791
[unsettling music playing]

00:45.333 --> 00:47.249
[Gayle King] We are here
with Verity Crawford

00:47.250 --> 00:48.665
at her home in Vermont,

00:48.666 --> 00:51.374
the place she shares with
her husband and the twins.

00:51.375 --> 00:53.540
I don't think there
are enough superlatives

00:53.541 --> 00:55.582
to describe this woman.
Let's pick one.

00:55.583 --> 00:59.582
Phenomenon, sensation, marvel.

00:59.583 --> 01:02.707
Uh, some would say "badass."
I'll go with that.

01:02.708 --> 01:05.332
You are considered one
of the bestselling authors

01:05.333 --> 01:06.499
on the planet.

01:06.500 --> 01:07.624
- Oh...
- Let's take that in

01:07.625 --> 01:08.749
for just a second.

01:08.750 --> 01:10.082
- "On the planet."
- Yes.

01:10.083 --> 01:12.540
Have you had time
to take it all in? What it...

01:12.541 --> 01:14.415
What it is like
to be able to provide

01:14.416 --> 01:17.124
such a beautiful life for
the people you love so much?

01:17.125 --> 01:20.624
To me, it's all a miracle.

01:20.625 --> 01:22.749
Yeah, but some could say...

01:22.750 --> 01:25.207
it's a miracle
built on villains.

01:25.208 --> 01:27.208
[dramatic music playing]

01:42.541 --> 01:45.333
[distant sirens wailing]

01:48.916 --> 01:51.750
[rattling]

01:57.916 --> 01:59.416
[bell dings]

02:06.041 --> 02:07.457
[Lowen] "I don't know
that anyone

02:07.458 --> 02:09.165
"named Louie Longsutter

02:09.166 --> 02:11.415
"could even be dangerous.

02:11.416 --> 02:13.790
"But the way
he stands there

02:13.791 --> 02:16.957
"just a little too close
to the edge of the porch,

02:16.958 --> 02:18.290
"like he's been
waiting for me

02:18.291 --> 02:19.665
"longer than he should have

02:19.666 --> 02:22.749
"makes me second-guess
my assumptions.

02:22.750 --> 02:27.124
"I try to imagine a serial
killer named Louie Longsutter.

02:27.125 --> 02:28.999
"I almost laugh
at the absurdity of it,

02:29.000 --> 02:30.707
"but being a woman

02:30.708 --> 02:33.749
"about to embark
on weeks of isolation,

02:33.750 --> 02:36.415
"the thought that he could
be a threat sticks in my mind.

02:36.416 --> 02:38.499
"Unwanted and uncomfortable."

02:38.500 --> 02:41.332
[cell phone rings]

02:41.333 --> 02:42.707
Sorry. Sorry.

02:42.708 --> 02:43.874
Sorry.

02:43.875 --> 02:46.165
Hi, hi.
No, I'm in a bookstore.

02:46.166 --> 02:47.708
Yeah, yeah,
this is a good time.

02:49.500 --> 02:50.707
[patron coughs]

02:50.708 --> 02:52.832
- [Lowen] <i>Hey.</i>
- Hey. How'd it go?

02:52.833 --> 02:54.499
I don't want to talk about it.

02:54.500 --> 02:56.415
Where were you? You said
you were gonna be here.

02:56.416 --> 02:57.665
[Corey] <i>You know
I wouldn't miss it</i>

02:57.666 --> 02:59.915
<i>if I didn't have
a good reason.</i>

02:59.916 --> 03:02.374
Hachette Book Group called.

03:02.375 --> 03:03.707
They wanna meet you.

03:03.708 --> 03:06.332
For what? Who... Who...
Who wants to meet me?

03:06.333 --> 03:07.707
[Corey] <i>They wouldn't say.</i>

03:07.708 --> 03:09.500
It's all very top secret.

03:10.166 --> 03:11.332
When?

03:11.333 --> 03:13.290
3:00 p.m. sharp.

03:13.291 --> 03:14.499
I'll meet you there, okay?

03:14.500 --> 03:16.624
Oh, please, and dress nice.

03:16.625 --> 03:18.499
<i>All right?</i>

03:18.500 --> 03:19.750
- Wait, Corey.
- [call disconnects]

03:21.666 --> 03:22.915
Wow.

03:22.916 --> 03:24.416
[horns honking]

03:27.250 --> 03:29.124
[distant sirens wailing]

03:29.125 --> 03:30.290
[machine drilling]

03:30.291 --> 03:33.749
[electronic pop music playing]

03:33.750 --> 03:36.708
[Lowen] <i>People like me belong
in overpopulated cities.</i>

03:41.583 --> 03:44.707
<i>In the tiny town
where I grew up,</i>

03:44.708 --> 03:47.041
<i>everyone knew
everything about everyone.</i>

03:51.958 --> 03:53.958
[Lowen] <i>But here,
I'm invisible.</i>

03:57.833 --> 03:59.208
[Lowen] <i>I like it that way.</i>

04:09.041 --> 04:10.207
[woman 1] Yo, mister,
watch out!

04:10.208 --> 04:11.415
[crashing]

04:11.416 --> 04:13.916
[all gasping and exclaiming]

04:15.166 --> 04:17.874
[woman 2] Oh, my God!
Oh, my God!

04:17.875 --> 04:19.082
[woman 3] A man
was riding his bike...

04:19.083 --> 04:20.499
- [man 1] He's not good.
- [woman 2] Hey?

04:20.500 --> 04:22.207
[woman 3] ...and a car
just came out of nowhere,

04:22.208 --> 04:23.416
- and it hit him.
- [man 1] Oh, my God.

04:25.208 --> 04:27.165
Oh, no.

04:27.166 --> 04:28.624
[man 2] There's been
a terrible accident.

04:28.625 --> 04:32.082
[stuttering] A bike messenger
was hit by a car.

04:32.083 --> 04:34.083
- [heart beating rapidly]
- [people clamoring]

04:40.250 --> 04:41.250
[muffled] Are you hurt?

04:43.500 --> 04:45.874
- [mumbles]
- Are you hurt?

04:45.875 --> 04:47.458
Is it on my face?

04:50.666 --> 04:51.999
There should be a bathroom
in this coffee shop

04:52.000 --> 04:53.332
over here, okay?

04:53.333 --> 04:54.958
[man 3] Look what you did!

04:57.083 --> 04:58.083
[Lowen coughs]

05:03.250 --> 05:05.540
- Oh...
- [knocking on door]

05:05.541 --> 05:07.708
[man] Hey, what are you doin'
in there? It's the men's room.

05:09.041 --> 05:10.291
[Jeremy] We'll be right out.

05:31.750 --> 05:33.333
Here, um...

05:34.125 --> 05:35.125
you can put this on.

05:37.291 --> 05:38.707
Thank you.

05:38.708 --> 05:39.708
[Jeremy] Of course.

05:44.958 --> 05:47.375
I can't tell
if you're calm or...

05:48.083 --> 05:49.250
if you're in shock.

05:51.750 --> 05:53.250
I don't know what I am.

05:57.583 --> 06:00.249
[sighs] Are you okay?

06:00.250 --> 06:02.624
[Jeremy] Uh, yeah.

06:02.625 --> 06:04.875
I've seen worse, unfortunately.

06:06.125 --> 06:07.416
Are you a doctor?

06:08.791 --> 06:10.291
[Jeremy] I'm in real estate.

06:13.166 --> 06:14.833
Or at least, I used to be.

06:17.083 --> 06:18.458
What happened to you?

06:21.041 --> 06:22.625
You really wanna know?

06:28.541 --> 06:30.124
I pulled my 8-year-old
daughter's body

06:30.125 --> 06:32.458
out of a lake last spring.

06:39.208 --> 06:40.791
I'm sorry.

06:42.708 --> 06:44.208
I'm sorry.

06:47.125 --> 06:49.500
My mom died last week.

06:50.625 --> 06:52.082
Oh...

06:52.083 --> 06:53.832
What happened to her?

06:53.833 --> 06:55.374
[Lowen] Uh, cancer.

06:55.375 --> 06:58.082
I was taking care of her
in my apartment.

06:58.083 --> 06:59.457
She died in there.

06:59.458 --> 07:02.416
In my apartment.
She died. Sorry.

07:05.625 --> 07:07.124
I have a meeting. I should...

07:07.125 --> 07:09.125
Yeah, me, too.

07:10.250 --> 07:11.665
Thank you for your help.

07:11.666 --> 07:12.916
Of course.

07:17.041 --> 07:18.041
[lock clicks]

07:19.416 --> 07:20.958
I'm Jeremy, by the way.

07:21.291 --> 07:22.500
Lowen.

07:34.125 --> 07:35.332
[door closes]

07:35.333 --> 07:36.750
God.

07:42.416 --> 07:44.332
[woman] Congratulations
on your bonus.

07:44.333 --> 07:45.333
[man] Thank you.

07:53.791 --> 07:55.874
- Hi.
- Hi. How can I help you?

07:55.875 --> 07:57.290
I'm here to see Amanda Thomas.

07:57.291 --> 07:59.415
- Okay.
- [Corey] Lowen.

07:59.416 --> 08:00.582
Hi. I'm sorry I'm late.

08:00.583 --> 08:02.666
You're not late.
You're on time.
